tom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T16:01:31-07:00","id":924152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pg. 98</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast may allow guests through any Burrow with a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> Intruders, on the other hand, must cope with any Tilts in effect and have to force their way through Burrows by spending a point of Willpower and succeeding on an Intelligence + Resolve roll contested by the Horror\u2019s Power + Resistance (see below). Forcing one\u2019s way through a Burrow takes half the Beast\u2019s Lair (round up) in turns, during which time the intruder is still subject to any Tilts in the Chamber he is trying to leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, for guests and the beast its reflexive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}